ets as radix digits (dice ⚀-⚅, card suits, chess, zodiac) | prebuilt tgt:glyph-radix | yes | one Unicode block, <=12 distinct glyphs, fixed-width groups | glyph -> index -> `radix_dec` rules | low-med |\n| 112 | skip / decimation cipher (read every k-th char mod n) | gap (gap skip-decimation) | yes (brute k, start) | anagram; no rail/columnar read | `c[i]=p[(s+i*k)%n]`, gcd(k,n)=1, invert | high: \"skip/hop/every Nth\" pun |\n| 113 | redefence (rail fence, rails read in key order) | gap (gap redefence) | yes (brute r! for r<=6) / title digits | anagram; rail reads come out in shuffled blocks | permute rails by key, then `rail_dec` | high: D18 sequel |\n| 114 | transposition stacked on a strict encoding (rail/columnar/reverse of a base64/hex/Morse STRING, or base64 of a rail-fenced text) | gap (gap transposition-over-strict) | yes | strict charset that refuses to decode, or decodes to an anagram | undo the outer layer, then the inner (peel with transposition pre-steps) | high: D16-17 stacking x D18 family |\n| 115 | word-level transposition (whole words rail-fenced/columnar/shuffled; per-word letter rail) | gap (gap word-transposition) | yes (brute) | every word English, order wrong; slug token intact | permute tokens by rail/columnar keys, crib gate | med-high |\n| 116 | riffle / perfect shuffle (in/out shuffle x k), odd-even split | gap (gap riffle-shuffle) | yes (brute k) | anagram; 2-rail reads half right | apply inverse shuffle k times | med: \"deck\"/\"shuffle\" pun |\n| 117 | double columnar / Myszkowski / keyed columnar with title word | prebuilt tgt:columnar (single key only); gap double-columnar-myszkowski | title | anagram; no keyless read works | `col_dec` twice; Myszkowski ties read together | med |\n| 118 | transposition + letter map stacked (rail of ROT13/Atbash/Caesar text, or vice versa) | gap (gap transposition-plus-letter-map) | yes | letters of the crib multiset NOT matching, but a rot/Atbash of it does | multiset test after each letter map, then transposition sweep | med-high: two seen families stacked |\n\n## Recognition cues (worker quick-reference)\n\n```\nKnown plaintext: \"Nice work decoding this warmup! To solve, submit this exact answer to the Game Master: a-b-c-NN\"\n word lengths: 4 4 8 4 6! 2 5, 6 4 5 6 2 3 4 6: slug   (exactly one \"!\", one \",\", one \":\")\n crib letters cover all but f j q y z; slug is ALWAYS lowercase -> lowercase case-losing decodes before submit\nSTEP 1 - lib first: python3 -c \"from lib import decode,warmups_codecs as w;t=open('blob.txt').read();\n  print(decode.decode_chunk(t)); print([n for n,e,d in w.CANDIDATES if d and w.SLUG.search(w.safe(d,t.strip()) or '')])\"\nSTEP 2 - charset fingerprint (python: sorted(set(t)), len(t), len(t)/110):\n [01] 8/7-groups .................. binary (D4); 4-groups -> nibbles->hex; 5-groups -> Bacon/Baudot; 0-blocks -> Chuck Norris\n [0-7] 3-digit ................... octal (D6);   [0-9] 32-126 tokens -> decimal (D5); 1-26 dashed -> A1Z26\n digit pairs, digits 1-5 only ..... Polybius / tap-code-digits;  . or x knock groups -> tap code\n digit runs of 2-9 repeats ........ multitap (44 33 555); single digits 2-9 per letter -> T9\n [0-9a-f] even, x2 ................ hex (D3); c1-e9/81-a9 + 40 -> EBCDIC cp037; 00 every 2nd byte -> UTF-16\n . - only (+ / or 3 spaces) ....... Morse (D16: output only 0-9A-F -> hex layer; digits -> char codes); 1/111 runs -> timing\n a/b (A/B) in 5s .................. Baconian (D17: all groups start `a` -> values 0-15 = HEX nibbles, 2 per byte);\n                                    values up to 25 -> letters; odd casing in cover text -> Bacon via case\n ANY 16-symbol output (0-9A-F, a-p only, 16 words) after a carrier = hex nibbles -> fromhex (D16, D17);\n   unknown 16 tokens -> map them by the crib hex `4e 69 63 65 20 77 6f 72 6b`. lib: twosym/bin4/aphex/tern/radix_dec\n 2-symbol groups of width 5/6 with values >15 -> base32/base64 INDEX;  ䷀.. hexagrams -> base64;  only space/TAB -> bits\n dotted quads / #RRGGBB / 4e69:6365 . IPv4 / colour / IPv6 bytes;  base64-ish that won't decode -> undo rev/rot13/atbash 1st\n only A D F G X (V) ............... ADFGX / ADFGVX (keyed: try title word + crib)\n only A C G T ..................... DNA 2-bit / codon\n %XX .............................. URL (D7);  &#..; -> HTML (D8);  \\uXXXX -> JSON (D9);  \\xNN -> C escape\n U+XXXX / %uXXXX / \\U0000XXXX ..... Unicode code-point notation -> chr(int(h,16))\n =XX tokens / soft \"=\\n\" .......... quoted-printable;  =?UTF-8?B?..?= -> MIME header\n A-Z2-7 (=) ....................... base32 (D10);  0-9A-V -> base32hex\n A-Za-z0-9+/ (=), len%4==0 ........ base64 (D1); starts H4sI -> gzip, eJ -> zlib inside (lib.decode.peel)\n A-Za-z0-9-_ no = ................. base64url (D11)\n [0-9A-Za-z] only, no pad ......... base62 (x1.34) / base36 if one case (x1.55)\n no 0 O I l + / = ................. base58 (x1.37)\n 0-9A-Z plus space $%*+-./: ....... base45 (x1.5)\n ! .. u (+z), maybe <~ ~> ......... ascii85;  RFC1924 set (no quotes , . / : [ \\ ]) -> base85; .-:+=^!/*?&<>()[]{}@%$# -> Z85\n ~all printable, no ' - \\ ......... basE91 (x1.23);  ! .. } minus \" ` -> base92\n begin 644 / lines start M or h ... uuencode / xxencode\n xn-- labels ...................... punycode/IDNA\nNON-ASCII:\n U+2800-28FF ⠝⠊⠉⠑ ................. Braille (⠼ = number sign)\n fullwidth Ｎｉｃｅ / math 𝐍𝐢𝐜𝐞 / ⓝ .. NFKC normalize\n ɐ q ɔ p ǝ ɟ ƃ ɥ ᴉ ʞ ɯ ɹ ʇ ʌ ʍ ʎ ...... upside-down (chepy from_upside_down, then maybe [::-1])\n CJK U+7Cxx, spaces kept .......... ROT8000 (chepy rot_8000)\n dense CJK/Hangul, no spaces ...... base65536/base2048;  all emoji 1 per byte -> base100\n invisible U+200B/C/D/2060/FEFF ... zero-width stego (count them: len(t) vs visible)\n ASCII-looking with odd bytes ..... homoglyphs (Cyrillic а е о р с х)\nSAME LENGTH, LETTERS ONLY CHANGE (word lengths 4 4 8 4 6! ... kept):\n best rot-N English ............... Caesar (D2 rot13, D14 +7); digits also shifted by 5 -> ROT18/ROT5\n mirror a<->z ..................... Atbash (D13)\n crib c-p constant ratio .......... affine (lib _fit_affine); constant per position mod k -> Vigenere key = (c-p)\n crib c+p periodic ................ Beaufort; no period but primer then plaintext -> autokey\n crib map consistent, not affine .. keyword substitution (21 letters from crib)\n neighbour keys (Muvr eptl) ....... QWERTY shift;  ;,.' in words -> Dvorak;  ALL printables shift -> ROT47 (D15)/ROT8000\nSAME CHARACTER MULTISET (anagram: one ! , :, slug digits intact) = TRANSPOSITION (D12 reverse, D18 rail 3):\n rail fence (D18: number in prompt = rails; w.rail_solve) | redefence | scytale/columnar (w.col_solve) | route/Caesar box\n | skip k | riffle | word order. Strip only \\r\\n (spaces are ciphertext); accept only text STARTING `Nice work`\nWORDS: Alfa Bravo -> NATO;  -ay endings -> Pig Latin;  N1c3 w0rk -> leet;  Ook./+-<>[] -> esoteric program\nTitle pun -> key: a cipher name + a number/word in the prompt = the key (D18 \"Three rails\"); verify on the crib.\nMastery: line k = day k's codec; keyed/transposed lines restart the key PER LINE (D18 line 18 = 6-8 char rail-3 slug\n tail). STACKS (D16-17): output hex/digits/b32/a-p -> decode AGAIN. Solver: return on the first full slug; slow fallbacks only on a miss.\n```\n\n## Readiness gaps\n\n```json\n[\n  {\"id\": \"transposition-sweep\", \"concept\": \"one keyless-transposition entry point: every permutation family in lib (reverse, rail r x offset, redefence, columnar/scytale widths, route, skip, riffle, word order), each also composed with reversal, crib-gated\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D18 opened the transposition family (rail 3). Add warmups_codecs.transposition_solve(blob): multiset test against crib+slug first (cheap reject), then enumerate keys family by family under a 0.5 s cap, accept only text that STARTS 'Nice work' and ends in a 3-word slug (rotated rail offsets contain the slug too). Fragment mode for Mastery (slug-tail gate, key restarts per line) and a register_free hook so a new day's transposition joins the joint search with one call. Strip only CR/LF: spaces are ciphertext. Fixtures: each family on the 110-B sentence + 6-8 char fragments.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"route-caesar-box\", \"concept\": \"route / Caesar box / spiral / boustrophedon (snake) / diagonal zigzag reads of a w x h grid\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Row 55. For every w,h with w*h >= len (pad 'x'/' '/'_' or none): write by rows, read by columns / spiral cw+ccw from each corner / snake rows / snake columns / diagonal (JPEG-style zigzag - fits the 'zigzag' vocabulary). Invert each read; crib-gated. CyberChef 'Caesar Box Cipher' = column read of a square-ish box. Fixtures single + fragment.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"skip-decimation\", \"concept\": \"skip cipher / decimation: ciphertext = every k-th plaintext char mod n\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"c[i] = p[(s + i*k) % n] for gcd(k,n)=1 (dcode 'Skip cipher'); brute k in 2..n-1, s in 0..n-1 with the crib prefix check (n~110 -> ~12k cheap tries; check the first 9 chars before building the rest). Also the non-coprime variant that wraps with +1 per lap. Pun cues: skip, hop, leap, every Nth, stride, step.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"redefence\", \"concept\": \"redefence: rail fence whose rails are emitted in a key order (rails permuted), optional offset\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Natural D18 sequel. r<=7 rails: brute r! orders x offsets (7! x 12 too many at full decode: check the crib prefix from the first rail positions only), key also from digits/words in the prompt ('3-1-2', 'THREE'). Reuse rail_rows to get rail lengths, slice the ciphertext in key order, then zigzag-read. Fixtures r=3..5.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"transposition-over-strict\", \"concept\": \"a transposition stacked on a seen strict encoding: rail/columnar/reverse of a base64/hex/base32/Morse STRING, or base64/hex of a rail-fenced sentence\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D16-17 stacked two layers; D18 introduced transposition. Cues: base64/hex/b32 alphabet that refuses to decode or has '=' mid-string; Morse/hex that decodes to an anagram of the crib. Add to peel: after a strict decode yields an anagram -> transposition_sweep; before a strict decode that fails -> try rail/columnar/rev on the encoded string (gate: strict decode must then succeed AND read crib). Under the 1 s cap.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"word-transposition\", \"concept\": \"word-level transposition: whole words rail-fenced / columnar / shuffled by a key, or each word's letters rail-fenced on their own\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Cue: every token is an English word (or an anagram of one), sentence order wrong, slug token intact or anagrammed. Tokens = space-split (16 crib words + slug); apply the transposition_sweep families at token level; per-word mode applies rail/reverse inside each word. Crib-gated.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"case-and-digit-loss\", \"concept\": \"case-losing / digit-losing codecs (Morse, NATO, Polybius, tap, Bacon, A1Z26, T9)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"Output must be lowercased; A1Z26/Polybius/Bacon/tap have no digit symbols, so slug digits are passed through literally or spelled - the decoder must keep non-alphabet tokens verbatim. decode_chunk Morse returns UPPERCASE. D16 confirmed the collapse direction: Morse output was UPPERCASE hex; lowercase only the FINAL text, and test the collapsed output for an inner hex/digit layer before lowercasing. D17: Bacon is case-free too and its letter reading (a-p) was a middle layer - same rule. The D17-night carrier decoders (twosym/bin4/aphex/tern/radix/chuck/dna) return lowercase-ready text; keep the rule for any new table carrier.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"transposition-mastery-joint\", \"concept\": \"short Mastery fragments under a transposition (6-8 chars, key restarts per line)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"D18 line 18 ('p-pr5e6' -> 'pper-56') has no charset cue; decode_chunked missed it and the solver added a slug-gated per-line rail pass. Any future transposition day: register its decoder as a free codec with its day number so _joint_free tries it on each unclaimed line; a 6-char fragment has few distinct rail/columnar reads, so the joined-text slug gate is the only arbiter.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"transposition-plus-letter-map\", \"concept\": \"transposition stacked with a seen letter map (rail fence of ROT13/Atbash/Caesar+7/ROT47 text, either order)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Cue: crib multiset test fails, but after rot13/atbash/rot-N/rot47 the multiset matches (letter maps commute with transpositions, so order does not matter for decoding). Run each FREE_CODECS map, re-test the multiset, then transposition_sweep. Fixtures: rail3(rot13), atbash(rail3), rail3(rot47).\"},\n  {\"id\": \"riffle-shuffle\", \"concept\": \"perfect riffle shuffle (in/out shuffle repeated k times), odd/even interleave\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"'deck'/'shuffle'/'cards' pun. Out-shuffle = interleave halves; in-shuffle starts with the second half; repeat k in 1..order (order of the permutation <= n). Decode = inverse permutation applied k times; crib-gated. Rail 2 offset 0 = one un-shuffle; make sure the sweep reports the right family name.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"double-columnar-myszkowski\", \"concept\": \"double columnar transposition and Myszkowski (repeated key letters read together), keys from title/prompt words\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"tgt:columnar covers single keyless widths + one title key. Add: same key twice, two different prompt words, Myszkowski tie rule; keys = every word/number of title+prompt and their uppercase/no-space forms; crib-gated; cap 0.5 s.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"affine-free-strict\", \"concept\": \"affine as a GM-confirmed-ready free codec\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"Already prebuilt (wc:affine + SPECULATIVE_FREE + _fit_affine). Risk is only bigram ranking vs rot-N/Atbash in Mastery joint assignment; confirm ratchet path registers it with a day number on first sight.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"chepy-cyberchef-cue\", \"concept\": \"standard-tool fallback for any unseen encoding\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"Workers should know chepy (venv) has from_base45/58/62/85/91/92/65536, rot_8000, from_upside_down, decode_zero_width, from_fullwidth, from_bacon, from_braille, from_nato, sms_decode_multitap, vigenere_decode, bifid_decode; CyberChef ops at tools/npm-cyberchef/node_modules/cyberchef/src/core/operations (run via the *_cyberchef.mjs pattern).\"},\n  {\"id\": \"bifid-std-square\", \"concept\": \"Bifid / Trifid with a STANDARD (keyless) square, period = full length or 5..10\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Row 75. Fractionation + transposition; keyless when the square is the plain A-Z (I=J) alphabet. Letters only change (spaces/punct kept or dropped), length kept, crib letters not a monoalphabetic map. pycipher Bifid/Delastelle; brute period; crib-gated. Trifid uses a 27-char alphabet (+ '.').\"},\n  {\"id\": \"base92\", \"concept\": \"base92\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"chepy from_base92 / CyberChef From Base92 decode it; cue = printable minus double-quote and backtick.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"base65536\", \"concept\": \"base65536 / base2048 / base32768\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"chepy from_base65536; others need pip (base2048) - install only if seen.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"bifid-adfgvx\", \"concept\": \"Bifid / Trifid / ADFGX / ADFGVX / Nihilist\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"pycipher implements all; key from title; ADFGX cue is the 5/6-letter alphabet.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"mime-encoded-word\", \"concept\": \"MIME encoded-word headers\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"email.header.decode_header handles =?charset?B|Q?...?=.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"esoteric\", \"concept\": \"Brainfuck / Ook! (Chuck Norris unary is prebuilt: chuck_dec)\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"No bf interpreter installed; a 20-line stdlib interpreter or pip 'brainfuck-interpreter' if one ever appears.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"misc-tables\", \"concept\": \"chemical symbols, Cetacean, Citrix CTX1 (DNA/codon, Roman, BCD, Gray, Kenny are prebuilt in warmups_codecs)\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"Recognition cues only; each is a lookup table the worker can write in one turn; CyberChef has From BCD and Cetacean Cipher Decode.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"homoglyph\", \"concept\": \"homoglyph (Cyrillic/Greek look-alike) substitution\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"unidecode/confusables not installed; NFKC does not fold Cyrillic. Install unidecode only if a day uses it.\"}\n]\n```\n","numLines":235,"startLine":1,"totalLines":235}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01LnLAZng472vnm7QGMNFFEU","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
