{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_014EQu4jCKCstUBi8ZfMHF31","type":"tool_result","content":"120:| Readable letters in the wrong order, ~110 B, exactly one `!` `,` `:`, spaces scattered (`N kcnhwuTo,b saae`); prompt names rails/zigzag/fence/a \n121:| Only `[0-9a-f]`, starts `fffe` (or `feff`), every other byte `00`, ~4 hex digits per char (prompt \"two bytes\", \"little\", \"endian\", \"wide\") | hex\n122:| Magic `PK\\x03\\x04` even if named `.txt` (mastery `blob-01.txt`) | `unzip -l`. It is a bundle of all sets `blob-01..NN.txt` |\n123:| Lines `01<TAB>...`, `02<TAB>...` | Strip the `NN\\t` prefix. Decode EACH line with its own encoding and concatenate without separators. Keep lead\n124:| Magic `1f8b`/`78`/`BZh`/`fd377a58` | gunzip / zlib / bzip2 / xz (in the toolbox. Not seen in the GM bytes yet) |\n125:| peel finds nothing | keyed/classical cipher: `lib.ciphers` (caesar_all, atbash, vigenere_crack, xor_crack, morse, base58, QP) |\n126:The generic path is `lib.decode.peel(data, accept)` (BFS over encodings) plus the day solvers in `challenges/day0N/warmups-*/solver/solve.py`. Eac\n127:\n128:## Day by day\n129:**Days 1-6** (base64, ROT13, hex, 8-bit binary, decimal, zero-padded octal): one layer each, solved in seconds-minutes.\n130:Lessons that still matter: D1 mastery failed ~12x because same-named `blob.txt` downloads overwrote each other (match by\n131:sha256); D3 mastery timed out when single letters/hex counted as English (score 2+-letter words, cap peel at 0.6 s); D4 a\n132:rot-N must beat the UNSHIFTED text by a margin (\"er:\" -> \"an:\"); D6 a shell `read` loop dropped the last token (no trailing\n133:newline), octal vs decimal = zero padding + lowercase share. Mastery from D2 on = ONE zip saved as `blob-01.txt`.\n134:\n135:**Days 7-9** (URL `%xx`, decimal HTML entities, quoted `\"\\u00XX\"` JSON string): one layer each, CORRECT in 18-53 s.\n136:Lessons that still matter: D7 mastery attempt 1 decoded the WHOLE zip (bundle saved as `blob-01.txt`, a name match\n137:returned the outer file) -> another set's slug fragment `py-storm-dune-80` -> incorrect; `lib.common.find_artifact` now\n138:returns the same-named member. D8 a `str.replace` solver patch silently matched nothing (assert anchors). D9 lib's `\\u`\n139:path is ASCII-only (`\\u00e9`, `\\n`, `\\\"` would fall through to rot-N garbage; not in GM bytes yet). Strict whole-fragment\n140:`%xx` and entity branches live in `lib.decode.decode_chunk`.\n141:\n142:**Days 10-13** (base32; unpadded base64url; reversed sentence; Atbash): one layer each, CORRECT in 5-73 s.\n143:Lessons that still matter: D11 `base64 -d`/strict len%4 b64 refused the unpadded blob and old `decode_chunk` fell through\n144:to rot-N garbage (re-pad first). D12 the carried-over solver answered in 5 s, but Mastery lost the timed attempt: a 28 s\n145:generic fallback, then 11/58 sets where rot-N \"decoded\" the reversed line 12 (`69-fove-n`). D13 the probe submitted a rot-N\n146:of Atbash text (`ovisx-tviskr-fbvecw-31`, rejected: gibberish words); Mastery 39/63 until free lines were assigned\n147:JOINTLY (`lib.decode._joint_free`, `FREE_CODECS`; each transform used once per blob).\n148:\n149:**Days 14-17** (Caesar +7; ROT47; Morse over hex; Bacon a/b 5-groups over hex): CORRECT in 4.5-39 s, first submit each day.\n150:Lessons that still matter: D14 Mastery set22 went MISSING when a rev/Atbash swap ended in a 2-word slug -> `caesar7` in\n151:`FREE_CODECS`, 3-word slug ranked first. D15 ROT47 (`tr '!-~' 'P-~!-O'`) is beyond rot-N/Atbash/reversal;\n152:`register_free(\"rot47\", 15, ...)`. D16 Morse whose symbols are only `0-9A-F` -> `fromhex` (first two-layer warmup). D17\n153:Bacon groups `aaaaa`-`abbbb` = nibbles; the answer-first worker read Bacon-26 letters (`a`-`p` only) then `ord-97` ->\n154:`fromhex` (~25 s). D17 Mastery (83 x 17) first run hit the harness's 60 s budget -- `answer()` ran the joint free-codec\n155:ranker on every set even after `decode_chunked`